&lt;p&gt;HawkEye 360 is equipping defense, intelligence, and national security leaders with mission-critical signals intelligence to enable faster, better decision making. By detecting, geolocating, and characterizing radio frequency emissions worldwide, HawkEye 360 delivers trusted domain awareness and early warning indicators to the US Government and allied partners. Our space-based collection, proprietary signal processing, and AI-powered analytics transform knowledge of RF spectrum into a strategic advantage. Proven by operational mission success, HawkEye 360 is redefining how signals intelligence strengthens national and global security.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;HawkEye 360 is committed to hiring and retaining a diverse workforce. We are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, marital status, national origin, age, veteran status, disability, or any other protected class.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;HawkEye 360 is looking for a Senior Communications Signals Analyst to join the Mission Engineering team. This role is responsible for advancing HawkEye 360’s communications signal intelligence capabilities by independently analyzing, interpreting, and validating complex RF communications signals derived from HawkEye 360 IQ data. The position blends deep technical expertise with hands-on signal analysis, product quality assurance, customer workflow support, and cross-team collaboration to shape both product strategy and collection platform requirements. As a primary point of contact for communications signal insights, demonstrations, and internal training, this role plays a critical part in driving product excellence and helping customers realize the full value of HE360’s communications signals offerings.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your main responsibilities will be:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently identify unknown communication signal external parameters using signals analysis tools for signals discovered within HE360 IQ data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently interpret specific communication signal standards documentation and conduct open source research to understand details of communications signals for signals discovered within HE360 IQ data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;With limited guidance, conduct analysis of unknown communication signals discovered within HE360 IQ data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct QA/QC of HE360 communications signals products by exercising common customer work flows, use cases, as well as writing automated test scripts when applicable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a POC for understanding common physics limitations/impacts to communications signals when using LEO collection platforms collecting signals in RF spectrum&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;With some guidance,&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;inform HE360 communications signals overall product vision and execution to include prioritization of specific communications technologies as well as product design and usability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;With some guidance, inform HE360 collection platform requirements to enable successful HE360 communications signal products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;With some guidance, conduct 3rd party communications signals product evaluations using HE360 IQ data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a primary POC for using and demonstrating the value of HE360 communications signals products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train other HE360 employees on how to use HE360 communications signals products when applicable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with HE360 SAs to tailor customer specific work flows using HE360 communications signals products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently conduct country-wide explorations for communications signals of interest using HE360 communications signals products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate vignettes for HE360 sales, product, and marketing teams to help showcase the value of HE360 communications signals products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your skills and qualifications:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential education and experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10 years of experience analyzing communications signals for government or military applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;STEM degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;completed 451, 452, MSAP and/or SADP courses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;experience working with docker &amp;amp; K8&#39;s&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scripting in Python or Bash&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with Linux&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;experience working with Airflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;experience working with GIS platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We offer a compensation package that includes a competitive base salary plus annual performance bonus and benefits. We consider many factors when determining salary offers, such as candidate&#39;s work experience, education, training &amp;amp; skills, as well as market and business considerations. We are also open to considering candidates with experience and qualifications at a different level than required in a job posting, which may affect the compensation package offered.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$130,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$175,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HawkEye 360 is equipping defense, intelligence, and national security leaders with mission-critical signals intelligence to enable faster, better decision making. By detecting, geolocating, and characterizing radio frequency emissions worldwide, HawkEye 360 delivers trusted domain awareness and early warning indicators to the US Government and allied partners. Our space-based collection, proprietary signal processing, and AI-powered analytics transform knowledge of RF spectrum into a strategic advantage. Proven by operational mission success, HawkEye 360 is redefining how signals intelligence strengthens national and global security.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;HawkEye 360 is committed to hiring and retaining a diverse workforce. We are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, marital status, national origin, age, veteran status, disability, or any other protected class.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly skilled &lt;strong&gt;Senior Export &lt;/strong&gt;Licensing&lt;strong&gt; &amp;amp; Compliance Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to lead our export control and trade compliance functions. In this role, you will manage the preparation and implementation of complex Technical Assistance Agreements (TAA) and DSP-5s, oversee compliance investigations, and prepare voluntary disclosures. You will act as the Company’s Empowered Official, the Company’s key liaison with the key government agencies involved in export licensing and compliance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your main responsibilities will be:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Licensing &amp;amp; Agreements:&lt;/strong&gt; Draft, submit, and manage complex international export licenses, Technical Assistance Agreements (TAA), and DSP-5s. Ensure adherence to all regulatory requirements, including government provisos and provisos-management protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance, Investigations &amp;amp; Disclosures:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage internal compliance policies, processes and procedures, conduct compliance investigations and root-cause analyses. Investigate, draft and submit voluntary disclosures to responsible regulatory administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agency Engagement:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the primary interface with the Directorate of Defense Trade Controls (DDTC), Defense Technology Security Administration (DTSA), and Bureau of Industry and Security (BIS).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Jurisdiction &amp;amp; Classification:&lt;/strong&gt; Perform jurisdiction and classification determinations for defense articles and defense services subject to the jurisdiction of the International Traffic in Arms Regulations (ITAR) and for and for equipment and technology subject to the Export Administration Regulations (EAR).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Provide expert guidance on complex export regulations to engineering, program management, Government relations and business development teams. Collaborate specifically on issues related to export policy and export control reforms, intelligence activities involving ELINT or COMINT and technical data/technology control plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your skills and qualifications:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential education and experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 5–8 years of direct, hands-on experience in trade compliance and export licensing, with a preference for specific experience with space business operations and technologies, and signals intelligence (SIGINT).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep, demonstrable experience with ITAR and EAR regulations, including voluntary disclosures and compliance investigations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agency Relations:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven track record of successfully interacting and managing submissions with DDTC, DTSA, and BIS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agreement Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Extensive expertise in preparing and managing TAAs and related licensing documents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Background:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience or technical exposure to SIGINT and Electronic Warfare (EW) systems, platforms, and related export challenges is highly desired.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security clearance (S, TS or TS/SCI) is a bonus.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; Preference will be given to candidates within commuting distance to Herndon, Virginia or willing to relocate to a location within commuting distance of Herndon, Virginia.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We offer a compensation package that includes a competitive base salary plus annual performance bonus and benefits. We consider many factors when determining salary offers, such as candidate&#39;s work experience, education, training &amp;amp; skills, as well as market and business considerations. We are also open to considering candidates with experience and qualifications at a different level than required in a job posting, which may affect the compensation package offered.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$185,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$230,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HawkEye 360 is equipping defense, intelligence, and national security leaders with mission-critical signals intelligence to enable faster, better decision making. By detecting, geolocating, and characterizing radio frequency emissions worldwide, HawkEye 360 delivers trusted domain awareness and early warning indicators to the US Government and allied partners. Our space-based collection, proprietary signal processing, and AI-powered analytics transform knowledge of RF spectrum into a strategic advantage. Proven by operational mission success, HawkEye 360 is redefining how signals intelligence strengthens national and global security.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;HawkEye 360 is committed to hiring and retaining a diverse workforce. We are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer, making decisions without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, marital status, national origin, age, veteran status, disability, or any other protected class.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;HawkEye&amp;nbsp;360 is seeking a&amp;nbsp;Sr. RF Electrical Engineer&amp;nbsp;on the Space Team. The Space Team’s mission is to design, build, and test small commercial satellites that provide revolutionary RF geospatial analytics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;You&amp;nbsp;will&amp;nbsp;perform&amp;nbsp;RF and electrical design of our space platforms with a primary focus on our&amp;nbsp;RF payloads. This includes&amp;nbsp;RF front ends,&amp;nbsp;integrating&amp;nbsp;Software Defined Radios (SDR’s)&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;antenna systems.&amp;nbsp;You’ll&amp;nbsp;define and execute RF performance tests&amp;nbsp;to verify mission requirements while also&amp;nbsp;developing analog, digital, and power electronics across our satellite platforms.&amp;nbsp;This role requires strong RF&amp;nbsp;and Electrical Engineering&amp;nbsp;expertise&amp;nbsp;working cross functionally with&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;mechanical, software, payload, and systems engineering&amp;nbsp;teams.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your main responsibilities will be:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and develop&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;RF payload architectures and Software Defined Radio systems for space-based RF collection missions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and optimize RF front ends, including filtering, amplification, frequency conversion, and signal conditioning circuitry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform electrical and RF simulations at a board and system level to validate the performance of different sub-systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform RF link budget analysis, interference modeling, and sensitivity trade studies to meet mission performance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support payload architecture decisions through mission-driven trade studies at PDR/CDR milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and scope RF performance test plans to verify key specifications including sensitivity, dynamic range, spurious emissions, linearity, and signal quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop test procedures and automation scripts to characterize SDR and RF front-end performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute EMI/EMC compliance testing and develop mitigation strategies for flight hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design digital, analog, and power electronics for satellite flight hardware. Create and review schematics, block diagrams, PCB layouts, and Design for Manufacturing (DFM).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with PCB Contract Manufacturers (CMs) to ensure quality control and timely delivery of flight hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support spacecraft integration and testing efforts, including the design of Electrical Ground Support Equipment (EGSE), flatsats for functional testing, and satellite flight hardware testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform first article hardware unit testing, including reception inspection, burn-in testing, thermal validation, and hardware checkouts.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
